@TITLE Adventureland
@AUTHOR Adapted from Scott Adams (1978)
@START meadow
@DESC_TEXT The first text adventure, reimagined.

@ROOM meadow
@DESC
You stand in a sunny
meadow. Tall grass sways
in a warm breeze. Paths
lead in every direction.
A stone altar sits among
the wildflowers.
@IF placed_eggs
Eggs glow on the altar.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go to the forest" -> forest
@CHOICE "Go to the lake" -> lakeside
@CHOICE "Go to the swamp" -> swamp
@CHOICE "Examine the altar" -> treasure_altar

@ROOM forest
@DESC
A dense forest of ancient
oaks. Shafts of light
pierce the canopy. Rusty
axe juts from a stump.
A path winds north to a
massive tree.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM axe "Rusty Axe" "A notched axe on a worn oak handle."
@CHOICE "Go to the big tree" -> tree_base
@CHOICE "Push through brush" -> quicksand
@CHOICE "Back to the meadow" -> meadow

@ROOM tree_base
@DESC
An enormous oak towers
above you. Its trunk is
wider than a house. Angry
bees swarm around a high
hollow. A knotted rope
hangs down.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Climb the rope" -> tree_top
@CHOICE "Back to the forest" -> forest

@ROOM tree_top
@DESC
You cling to the oak's
crown, wind whipping your
hair. A nest of leathery
eggs sits in a crook of
branches. Bees swarm the
honeycombs above.
@IF bees_calm
The bees drift lazily.
Sweet honey drips from
golden combs in reach.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@ITEM dragon_eggs "Dragon Eggs" "Three speckled eggs, warm to the touch."
@CHOICE "Smoke bees with mud" -> tree_calm @NEED mud
@CHOICE "Grab honey bare" -> bee_sting @NEED !bees_calm
@CHOICE "Climb down" -> tree_base

@ROOM tree_calm
@DESC
You smear swamp mud on a
branch and light it. Warm
smoke billows up. Bees
retreat to the far side
of the canopy, docile
at last.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET bees_calm
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Back to the tree top" -> tree_top_calm @USE mud

@ROOM tree_top_calm
@DESC
Bees drift lazily above,
no longer a threat now.
Sweet honey drips from
golden combs. The dragon
egg nest sits nearby. The
view stretches for miles.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM honey "Wild Honey" "A sticky comb of fragrant golden honey."
@ITEM dragon_eggs2 "Dragon Eggs" "Three speckled eggs, warm to the touch."
@CHOICE "Climb down" -> tree_base

@ROOM bee_sting
@DESC
Bees attack in a furious
cloud. Stings cover your
hands and face. You lose
your grip and tumble from
the tree.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "The bees were too fierce. Perhaps smoke would calm them."

@ROOM lakeside
@DESC
A crystal lake stretches
before you. Golden fish
dart beneath the surface.
A rocky ledge juts over
the water to the east.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Catch a fish" -> lake_fall @NEED !has_net
@CHOICE "Walk to the ledge" -> ledge
@CHOICE "Back to the meadow" -> meadow

@ROOM lake_fall
@DESC
You lunge at a golden
fish but they dart away.
You overbalance and fall
into freezing water. The
current pulls you under.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "The lake is deeper than it looks. You needed a net."

@ROOM ledge
@DESC
A narrow rocky ledge over
the lake. Far below, the
water shimmers. Carved in
the rock is a crude arrow
pointing down. It says
"GROVE" beneath it.
@IF mirror_used
You recall the mirror's
vision of a hidden grove!
This must be the way.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Climb down cliff" -> hidden_grove @NEED mirror_used
@CHOICE "Back to the lake" -> lakeside

@ROOM swamp
@DESC
Murky water bubbles among
cypress stumps. The air
is thick with rot. Dark
mud oozes everywhere.
Gnarled roots form a way
underground.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM mud "Swamp Mud" "A handful of thick, pungent swamp mud."
@CHOICE "Go underground" -> root_chamber
@CHOICE "Back to the meadow" -> meadow

@ROOM quicksand
@DESC
The ground gives way! You
sink into quicksand up to
your waist. It pulls at
you with a cold grip that
tightens every second.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Pull free slowly" -> forest
@CHOICE "Struggle wildly" -> quicksand_death

@ROOM quicksand_death
@DESC
Your thrashing only makes
it worse. The quicksand
closes over your head.
The forest falls silent.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "You sank beneath the quicksand. Move slowly next time."

@ROOM root_chamber
@DESC
Twisted tree roots form
the ceiling of this cave.
Iron-rich water seeps
down the walls. Passages
branch in three ways.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM keys "Iron Keys" "A ring of heavy iron keys, cold to the touch."
@CHOICE "Go to the alcove" -> lamp_alcove
@CHOICE "Go deeper" -> pit_top
@CHOICE "Up to the swamp" -> swamp

@ROOM lamp_alcove
@DESC
A small alcove carved
from the earth. A shelf
holds a battered oil lamp
still full of fuel. Tally
marks scratch the walls.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM lamp "Oil Lamp" "A sturdy brass lamp with a bright flame."
@ON_ENTER @SET has_lamp
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Back to root chamber" -> root_chamber

@ROOM pit_top
@DESC
You stand at the edge of
a yawning pit. Darkness
swallows all light below.
A rough ladder descends
into the void. Cool air
rises from the depths.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Descend with lamp" -> pit_descent @NEED has_lamp
@CHOICE "Descend in the dark" -> pit_dark @NEED !has_lamp
@CHOICE "Go back" -> root_chamber

@ROOM pit_dark
@DESC
You climb down blind.
Your foot slips on a wet
rung. You fall, tumbling
through darkness until
the ground finds you.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "It is pitch dark. You needed a lamp."

@ROOM pit_descent
@DESC
Your lamp flickers as you
climb down the rusty iron
ladder. At last your feet
touch solid ground. A dim
chamber opens before you.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Look around" -> pit_bottom

@ROOM pit_bottom
@DESC
The lamp reveals a rough
chamber at the pit base.
An iron door is set into
the far wall, locked. Old
bones litter the floor.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Unlock the door" -> antechamber @NEED keys
@CHOICE "Climb back up" -> pit_top

@ROOM antechamber
@DESC
An ornate hallway. Faded
tapestries line the wall.
A burly guard in rusted
armor blocks the passage,
his spear raised.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET door_unlocked
@CHOICE "Offer the honey" -> guard_bribed @NEED honey
@CHOICE "Fight the guard" -> guard_fight
@CHOICE "Go back" -> pit_bottom_open @USE keys

@ROOM guard_fight
@DESC
You charge the guard. He
sidesteps easily and
strikes you down with the
blunt end of his spear.
Far too strong for you.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "The guard is too strong. Perhaps a gift would work."

@ROOM guard_bribed
@DESC
The guard's eyes light up
at the sight of honey. He
takes it and steps aside,
licking his fingers. A
grand doorway awaits.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET guard_fed
@SCORE +35
@CHOICE "Enter throne room" -> royal_chamber @USE honey

@ROOM pit_bottom_open
@DESC
The iron door stands open
now. The rough chamber is
quiet. The ladder leads
back up.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go through the door" -> antechamber
@CHOICE "Climb back up" -> pit_top

@ROOM royal_chamber
@DESC
A vaulted throne room
carved from living rock.
Crystals in the ceiling
catch your lamp, casting
rainbows. A jeweled crown
rests on the throne.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM crown "Royal Crown" "A platinum crown set with blood-red rubies."
@CHOICE "Search behind throne" -> treasury @NEED mirror_used
@CHOICE "Go back" -> antechamber_clear

@ROOM antechamber_clear
@DESC
The hallway is quiet now.
The guard sits content in
a corner, still savoring
honey. The throne room
lies to the north.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go to throne room" -> royal_chamber
@CHOICE "Back to the pit" -> pit_bottom_open
@CHOICE "Examine the mirror" -> mirror_room

@ROOM mirror_room
@DESC
Set into the wall is an
ancient mirror framed in
tarnished silver. Its
surface ripples like
water though no breeze
stirs the air.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Look in the mirror" -> mirror_vision
@CHOICE "Go back" -> antechamber_clear

@ROOM mirror_vision
@DESC
The mirror clouds, then
clears. You see a hidden
grove beneath a ledge by
a lake. Then a treasury
behind a throne, veiled
by illusion. You know
the secret paths now.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET mirror_used
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Step back" -> mirror_room

@ROOM treasury
@DESC
Behind the throne, hidden
by ancient magic, a small
vault gleams. A gold
scepter stands in a case
of crystal, untouched
for centuries.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM scepter "Gold Scepter" "A scepter of pure gold topped with a sapphire."
@SCORE +15
@CHOICE "Back to throne room" -> royal_chamber

@ROOM hidden_grove
@DESC
You climb down to a grove
hidden beneath the ledge.
Luminous moss coats the
stones. A golden net lies
on a branch, shimmering
with enchantment.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM golden_net "Golden Net" "A net woven from threads of pure gold."
@ON_ENTER @SET has_net
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Back to the meadow" -> meadow

@ROOM treasure_altar
@DESC
A weathered stone altar
stands in a clearing.
Ancient runes ring its
base. Four shallow pits
mark its surface, each
shaped for an offering.
@IF placed_eggs
Eggs glow in the first
hollow, pulsing warmth.
@ENDIF
@IF placed_crown
The crown gleams in the
second hollow.
@ENDIF
@IF placed_net
The golden net fills the
third hollow with light.
@ENDIF
@IF placed_scepter
The scepter shines in
the last hollow.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Place dragon eggs" -> altar_eggs @NEED dragon_eggs
@CHOICE "Place the crown" -> altar_crown @NEED crown
@CHOICE "Place golden net" -> altar_net @NEED golden_net
@CHOICE "Place the scepter" -> altar_scepter @NEED scepter

@ROOM altar_eggs
@DESC
You set the warm eggs
into the first hollow.
They fit perfectly. The
runes around them begin
to glow with a faint
amber light.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET placed_eggs
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Back to the altar" -> treasure_altar @USE dragon_eggs

@ROOM altar_crown
@DESC
The crown settles into
the second depression.
Ruby light joins the
amber glow. The altar
vibrates beneath your
hands.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET placed_crown
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Back to the altar" -> treasure_altar @USE crown

@ROOM altar_net
@DESC
The golden net flows into
the third hollow like
liquid metal. A third
light joins the chorus.
The runes pulse faster.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET placed_net
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Back to the altar" -> treasure_altar @USE golden_net

@ROOM altar_scepter
@DESC
You place the scepter in
the final hollow. All
four lights blaze upward
in a pillar of white fire
The earth trembles. A
voice booms from above.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET placed_scepter
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Listen to the voice" -> victory @USE scepter

@ROOM victory
@DESC
"ADVENTURER! YOU HAVE
GATHERED THE FOUR LOST
TREASURES AND RESTORED
THEM TO THEIR RIGHTFUL
PLACE. THE LAND IS MADE
WHOLE AGAIN."

Light fills the meadow.
Flowers bloom where the
altar stood. You have
won Adventureland!
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +20
@WIN "You restored the four treasures! Score: {score}"
